        "width": 460,
        "height": 784,
        "content": "## Any File to JSON Converter\n\nTurns any file a workflow receives into clean JSON: images, PDFs, spreadsheets, JSON, text documents and web pages. Call it from any workflow that handles attachments or Drive files, and get one predictable result per file.\n\n### How it works\n1. A parent workflow sends binary files, or a URL, plus an optional `extraction` object naming the fields it wants.\n2. Each file becomes its own item, and a JSON Schema is built from `extraction.field_schemas`.\n3. Files are routed by MIME type: images go to a vision LLM, everything else to native text extraction.\n4. If fields were requested, an LLM turns the text into JSON matching them.\n5. Every file returns `{status, error, data: {text, content_class, class_confidence}}`. `status` is `ok`, or `unsupported` when no route matches.\n6. A step that fails (corrupt PDF, unreachable URL) fails the run, so the parent's error workflow sees it. To keep going per file, set the parent's Execute Workflow node to continue on error.\n\n### Setup steps\n- [ ] Add a **vision-capable LLM** credential to **Vision LLM**\n- [ ] Add an **LLM** credential to **Text LLM** (a free tier works)\n- [ ] Save and **publish**: parents run the published version\n- [ ] In the parent, add an **Execute Workflow** node pointing at this workflow, passing `binary_files` and an optional `extraction`\n\n### Customization\n- Support a new MIME type in **Route by File Type**. Pick the branch by what it can decode, not by the label.\n- `class_confidence` (0-1) lets the parent auto-accept, review or flag each result. See [confidence scoring](https://github.com/runfish5/micro-services/blob/main/projects/n8n/docs/observability-through-llm-confidence-estimate.md).\n\n[Node-by-node docs](https://github.com/runfish5/micro-services/blob/main/projects/n8n/03_any-file2json-converter/workflows/mainflow.md) \u00b7 Used by [smart-folder2table](https://github.com/runfish5/micro-services/blob/main/projects/n8n/02_smart-table-fill/workflows/smart-folder2table.json) and [inbox-attachment-organizer](https://github.com/runfish5/micro-services/blob/main/projects/n8n/04_inbox-attachment-organizer/README.md)"
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
